---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const locale = "en";
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Privacy, source, and update policies for Learning Atlas." current="About" locale={locale}>
  <section class="section about-panel"><div class="container split"><article class="prose profile-panel"><p class="eyebrow">Policy</p><h1>About this site</h1><p class="lead">Learning Atlas is a backend-free static site built with Astro and TypeScript for future free GitHub Pages hosting.</p><h2>Privacy and progress</h2><p>Lesson completion status is stored only in this browser's localStorage. There is no server, account, cross-device sync, or external API call for learning behavior. If local storage is blocked, the page says so and remains readable.</p><h2>Source policy</h2><p>Lessons are original study notes with official links for further reading. Project pages are based on public GitHub READMEs and are not run or independently re-tested here. Third-party sources keep their own licenses; this site's MIT license covers original site code only.</p><p>Study notes are not full certification courses. Identity, governance, monitoring, and continuity appear across infrastructure topics; AI and ML are extended learning and do not claim complete coverage of the three AZ exams.</p><h2>Hugging Face status</h2><p>A personal Hugging Face profile or project has not been confirmed, so it is not listed. The resources page only links to Hugging Face Learn as a general learning entry.</p><h2>Update guide</h2><p>Add lessons under src/content/lessons with slug, track, tags, sourceUrls, reviewedAt, locale, and order. Pages, sitemap, and search are generated from content. New projects need public sources and clear boundaries between design intent, repository self-description, and verified facts.</p></article><aside class="sidebox"><h3>Publication scope</h3><ul><li>Static HTML/CSS/JS only.</li><li>No external fonts, CDN, runtime model calls, or backend.</li><li>MIT license covers original site code only.</li></ul></aside></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
